<title>USA: PACE PROPERTY AUTH, FLA., REPRICED, YIELDS RAISED.</title>
<headline>PACE PROPERTY AUTH, FLA., REPRICED, YIELDS RAISED.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Union Capital Markets Corp. said Wednesday it repriced/restructured Pace Property Finance Authority $13 million deal. Raising yields in several maturities and also raising the par amount from $12.860 million to $13.160 million.</p>
<p>The repricing/restructure follows:</p>
<p>PACE PROPERTY FINANCE AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $13,160,000*</p>
<p>(SANTA ROSA CO., FL)</p>
<p>UTILITY SYSTEM IMPROVEMENT &amp; REFUNDING REVENUE</p>
<p>SERIES 1997</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE THESE BONDS ARE SUBJECT TO FLORIDA INTANGIBLES TAX.</p>
<p>WE HAVE THE VERBAL AWARD. THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED. WE ARE LONG</p>
